  "summary": "# Daily Health-Tech Digest — November 12, 2026\n\nThe regulatory and competitive landscape is shifting rapidly across multiple fronts. The FDA's approval of Merck KGaA's Pimjetmi for rare tumors continues the company's focused acquisition strategy, while Maven Clinic's expansion into 475 health plans signals growing mainstream adoption of virtual care infrastructure. More significantly, Democrats' midterm victories could reshape healthcare policy around affordability and access, and incoming congressional chairs are already investigating most-favored-nation drug pricing agreements—prompting some drugmakers to reconsider international launch strategies to protect U.S. revenues.\n\nOn the AI front, two parallel narratives are emerging: innovation is accelerating with new tools like Google Cloud's Gemini for healthcare and MDCalc's CrossCover verification system, but the field is also grappling with trust and safety concerns. The All of Us study's identification of thousands of new drug-response genetic variants underscores precision medicine's potential, while proposals to revamp obesity diagnosis could flip millions of patients' diagnoses and treatment paths. Public health concerns are mounting as well, with the U.S. at risk of losing its measles elimination status and ethics questions surfacing around conflicts of interest on preventive care panels.",
